\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The modular decomposition does not use averaging}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{At #{p=3}, the group order #{24} is zero in the
coefficient field, so division by the group order
cannot define a normalized average. The two-column
decomposition in \ref{fdip-00VW} is instead a
specific direct-sum decomposition proved by an
algebra isomorphism and an explicit map. Its
existence does not assert semisimplicity of every
#{\mathbb F_3[2T]}-module.}

\p{Mathlib's averaging ingredient
\leanref{LinearMap.equivariantProjection_condition}
requires the group order to be a unit and starts
with a linear retraction. Those hypotheses are
separate from the native column calculation.
No whole coupled-module theorem is supplied by
that declaration.}

\p{The internal columns of \ref{fdip-00VW} are
preserved for every link field. The geometric
projector of \ref{fdip-00VO} acts on the exterior
factor and fails on its displayed one-site
background. The two assertions concern different
tensor factors.}
